WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  protesters defied a mandatory curfew  president pedro castillo imposed the  measure late on monday protesters said  it infringed on their freedom police  tried to contain the people's anger  they used tear gas as thousands of  peruvians demanded castillo's  resignation  many had come to rally peacefully with  children and the elderly joining the  demonstrations  antonio portugal says he'll protest  until castillo is ousted  i'm so angry we cannot have this kind of  a president we have to put pressure on  him to live and to live now  stores schools and markets remained  closed for most of the day the army was  deployed to some districts pedro  castillo was under pressure and lifted  the curfew six hours before it was due  to end  the spike in fuel food and fertilizer  prices was too much even for the  president's former supporters  poor peruvians whose hopes were raised  when he came to power last year are now  turning their backs on the government  the truth is that castillo has to leave  because he's inept this is not a  government out with him  the president met lawmakers to find a  solution to the crisis but left without  announcing any plan  the situation is getting more tense in  the streets of the capital as the hours  go by with protesters throwing rocks at  police and police responding with tear  gas now these are a series of protests  that began a week ago and many believe  that they will continue  [Music]  whatever castillo decides to do next  protesters here say they are fed up with  a president who's not fit to govern  mariana sanchez al jazeera lima peru

